{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 49, :comments ["<b>To this mountain of the Avarim, Mount Nevo.</b> It is called the mountain of the Avarim because this mountain was open to two sides (עברים) — toward the road of Kadesh and toward Mount HaHor where the graves of the brothers are. And I have already mentioned this in the section (Numbers 13) of זאת חקת התורה." "<b>Which faces Jericho.</b> We find in the Torah ירחו with a ציר\"י and without a יו\"ד, and in Joshua it is written יריחו with a יו\"ד. And it is possible to say the reason for the matter: that the word ירחו with a ציר\"י is from the word ירח, and it is a word encompassing tiferet and kavod, for Moses attained the moon together with the vav, but in Joshua, whose prophecy is from the יו\"ד like all the other prophets, he wrote יריחו with a יו\"ד to explain that a fragrance reached him and was drawn from the יו\"ד which draws from the וי\"ו, and this is clear."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:38.753948292Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}